    {
      "name": "update_prd_section",
      "description": "Change one section of a PRD after it was created: scope (nonGoals, outOfScope), assumptions, open questions, risks, edge cases (what can go wrong and what should happen), security considerations, design guidance, external dependencies, technical requirements and contracts (including permissions and compliance), global acceptance criteria, constraints, rollout and measurement plans, or the introduction, problem and solution. For risks, edge cases and security, think adversarially: assume things fail and that someone is actively trying to abuse the feature, and write down the specific failure or attack with what should happen.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
